## 7. Migration 006 — RPC Functions

All analytics queries that aggregate data are implemented as PostgreSQL functions and called via `supabase.rpc()`. This avoids pulling raw rows to the client and summing in Dart.

All functions are `SECURITY DEFINER` with `STABLE` or `VOLATILE` markers. They read `auth.uid()` internally so callers cannot pass a different user ID — RLS equivalent at the function level.

```sql
-- supabase/migrations/20240101000006_rpc_functions.sql

-- ============================================================
-- get_daily_nutrition_totals
-- Returns summed macros for each day in a date range.
-- Used by: CaloriesChart, MacrosChart, DailyLog aggregation.
-- ============================================================

CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION get_daily_nutrition_totals(
  p_from DATE,
  p_to   DATE
)
RETURNS TABLE (
  log_date      DATE,
  total_kcal    NUMERIC,
  total_protein NUMERIC,
  total_carbs   NUMERIC,
  total_fat     NUMERIC,
  entry_count   INT
)
LANGUAGE SQL
STABLE
SECURITY DEFINER
AS $$
  SELECT
    fl.log_date,
    ROUND(SUM(fl.calories_kcal), 1)  AS total_kcal,
    ROUND(SUM(fl.protein_g), 1)       AS total_protein,
    ROUND(SUM(fl.carbs_g), 1)         AS total_carbs,
    ROUND(SUM(fl.fat_g), 1)           AS total_fat,
    COUNT(*)::INT                      AS entry_count
  FROM public.food_logs fl
  WHERE fl.user_id = auth.uid()
    AND fl.log_date >= p_from
    AND fl.log_date <= p_to
  GROUP BY fl.log_date
  ORDER BY fl.log_date;
$$;

COMMENT ON FUNCTION get_daily_nutrition_totals IS
